data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Verification Protocols**\n\nI'm now establishing verification protocols, tagging claims as either established knowledge ([Savoir]), recall ([Cité de mémoire]), or inference ([Supposition]). Each number is cited, prioritizing transparency. I'm removing unverified numbers.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 20415,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 19827,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","responseId": "2gMDa-blDJbmwbUPm4_kqQ0"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Claim Differentiation**\n\nI'm now separating \"Ce qui est mesuré\" from \"Ce qui est raconté\" in my analysis of discovery. I'm focusing on contrasting the empirical evidence with discoverer accounts and historical narratives. This includes detailed analysis of branching processes, networks, and combinatorial growth, integrating diverse data sources and methodologies.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 20708,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 20120,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","responseId": "2gMDa-blDJbmwbUPm4_kqQ0"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Integration Framework**\n\nI'm now separating analytical frameworks into what's measured empirically versus the reported accounts of discovery. This will facilitate comparing diverse data such as lab observation, neuroscience limits, and the statistical physics of neutral networks. The goal is to provide a comprehensive view by analyzing both distinct knowledge domains and the unstated consequences of published work.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 20936,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 20348,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","responseId": "2gMDa-blDJbmwbUPm4_kqQ0"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Refining Cost Comparisons**\n\nI'm now refining my approach to comparing falsification costs, focusing on computational experiments, particularly with zero-cost LLMs, fuzzing, and data analysis using OpenAlex and Lean Mathlib. The goal is to show the cost advantages of these methods in comparison to wet-lab ethnography and grant audits. I'm focusing on contrasting experimental results with ethnographic and audit costs.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 21210,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 20622,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","responseId": "2gMDa-blDJbmwbUPm4_kqQ0"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Verifying Cited Percentiles**\n\nI've just confirmed the exact meaning of \"top 5%\" in Uzzi et al. (2013), and clarified citation accuracy for Lean and Mikolov et al.'s work in context. All sources are now precisely verified for accurate inclusion.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 21532,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 20944,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-carbon","responseId": "2gMDa-blDJbmwbUPm4_kqQ0"}

